iio: imu: add Qualcomm SSC IMU (sns_client over QRTR) driver

New IIO driver exposing the accelerometer and gyroscope managed by the
Snapdragon Sensor Core sensor framework ("SEE") on the ADSP. On SM8750
there is no SLPI; the SSC and the ICM-4x6xx driver live inside the ADSP
firmware and are reached through the sns_client QMI service (id 400) on
QRTR, whose payload is a protobuf sns_client request/event stream.

The driver is an in-kernel QMI client (qmi_helpers): it lookup-tracks the
service (which appears only after a userspace FastRPC daemon serves the
sensor registry to the PD, possibly long after boot, and across ADSP
restarts), discovers the accel/gyro SUIDs, enables continuous streaming,
and pushes samples into a standard IIO kfifo buffer. A small hand-rolled
protobuf codec encodes the requests and decodes the float sample events;
IEEE-754 values are converted to micro-SI integers without using the FPU.

Channels: accel x/y/z (IIO_ACCEL), anglvel x/y/z (IIO_ANGL_VEL), soft
timestamp. Raw values are micro-m/s^2 and micro-rad/s (scale 1e-6).
Sample rate is settable via sampling_frequency (default 100 Hz).

Wired in as a faux_device (no DT node; the QRTR service is the resource).

